  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">EXPO Circular Building Mission in Osaka</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This activity supported Dutch participation in a circular building mission to the World Expo in Osaka, with the aim of expanding the circular economy network in the Osaka and Kansai regions. CERF activities included a session reflecting on previous circular economy cooperation between Japan and the Netherlands, where stakeholders explored ways to accelerate the circular transition and continue bilateral collaboration. A visit to Kobe also facilitated knowledge exchange on architecture and construction practices and identified opportunities for cooperation.The Osaka Kansai Expo 2025 increased regional awareness of circular economy approaches in the built environment and stimulated further interest in the topic. In addition, the Dutch Expo pavilion initiated the registration of its construction materials in Madaster in preparation for relocation, contributing to the further development of the Madaster Japan partnership involving Madaster, Taisei Corporation, Keio University and Asanuma Corporation.Remark Due to the transparency with regard to the IATI projects, a non-ODA country has been included in this project.</narrative>
  </description>
